# Simulate > Drag "CFD table": a flight flies on the stored drag table and, when a fresh 3D stability solve rides on it, on that
# solve's normal force and CP. The results show "Min margin in flight" (with the Mach where it occurs and the RASAero II guidance
# chip) and the labels read `· CFD (3D)`. The drive scripts cannot wait on real solves (minutes on a GPU), so the document is the
# example with hand-made CFD tables (Extended's own values with a one-caliber CP dip at Mach 1; not a solver result):
#   BOWSHOCK_FLIGHT_LIFT_FIXTURE=/tmp/example-flight-lift.bowshock cargo test -p bowshock -- --ignored the_flight_lift_fixture
#   BOWSHOCK_OPEN=/tmp/example-flight-lift.bowshock cargo run --release -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/cfd-flight-lift.drive out/cfd-flight-lift
viewport 1300x800
click "Simulate"

# On Extended: the margin comes from the build-up. "Bigger motor" (I284W) is the example flight that gets into the transonic range.
click (60, 232)
click (17, 94)
click (17, 226)
click "Run"
click "Stability"
move (700, 300)
move (702, 302)
screenshot flight-extended-dark.png

# On the CFD table: drag and stability from the tables.
click "CFD table"
click "Run"
move (700, 300)
move (702, 302)
screenshot flight-lift-dark.png
click "Light"
move (700, 300)
move (702, 302)
screenshot flight-lift-light.png
